Test B (thread 2): in test_factoryState.js — scoring. Scenario 1: head has quality.yml (ciWorkflow, path match) terminal success + fresher unrelated non-dispatch run (e.g. labeler, event push) terminal success → cite = quality.yml run (score 2 beats fresher score 1). Under current code: freshest wins → labeler steals cite → RED. Scenario 2 (in-flight preference): quality.yml active + labeler terminal green → cite = quality.yml (in flight). Hmm — is that a behavior I want to lock? Per Option A yes. Scenario 3: only unrelated non-dispatch runs → still cites (score 1 fallback, residual risk documented) — that's the documented tradeoff, assert it stays citable? That's the fail-open behavior — worth a test to pin the documented tradeoff. Also non-dispatch repo CI still cited when it's the only real run (existing tests probably cover).

