- Option A: cite = quality.yml in flight → pr_validation lane lights (true: machine validation IS in flight). Good.
- Option B: cite = labeler green → shows green cite from unrelated workflow while real validation in flight. Worse (misleading: green from nothing real).

Option A is better for board honesty. Also the reviewer's core complaint #1 was a fresher score-1 STEALING from score-2 — both options fix that. Complaint #2 "light pr_validation while only an unrelated workflow is queued": only-an-unrelated-queued = no score-2 run at all → tier 2 empty → fall to tier 1 → active score-1 → still lights. Neither option fully fixes #2 without breaking the fail-open dynamic-validation case (dynamic per-PR validation = non-dispatch = score 1, MUST be able to light pr_validation while in flight). So #2 is inherently part of the documented tradeoff — the comment must own it. 

So: implement Option A — score tier first, then terminal-before-active within the winning tier? Hmm wait, careful: within tier 2, if there are BOTH terminal and active runs, terminal wins (existing semantics preserved). Within tier 2, if only active → active cite. Then tier 1 consulted only if tier 2 has NO candidate at all. Let me restructure:

