Wait — decision: within a tier terminal-before-active, but ACROSS tiers does score-2-active beat score-1-terminal? With the structure above: `bestRun(terminal pool)` first — if ANY terminal real run exists (any score), it wins over active. So score-1 terminal beats score-2 active. That's Option B (terminal-first globally).

Hmm, I earlier leaned Option A (tier first, then terminal). Let me think about which scenario matters:

Scenario X: quality.yml (score 2) re-run in flight after previous quality.yml failure. Terminal pool = old quality.yml failure (score 2). Active pool = quality.yml in flight (score 2). Same tier → terminal wins → cite = failure. Pre-existing gh-816 behavior (terminal first). Both options agree here (same tier).

Scenario Y: quality.yml first-ever dispatch in flight (score 2 active) + stale unrelated labeler green from an earlier head... wait, runs are filtered to head_sha === sha — same head. Unrelated labeler run on THIS head green (score 1 terminal) + quality.yml on this head in flight (score 2 active).
