💡 **SUGGESTION (thread 3) — fixed: carried records with no landed conclusion are marked `carried: true`**

Took the "keep it with an explicit `carried: true` marker" option — dropping the record would erase the audit trail `merged_recent` persistence exists to keep, while the marker lets the board render it as unverified rather than live:

```js
var mergedChecks = (pr.head && pr.head.sha &&
        headVerdict(pr.head.sha)) || null;
if (!mergedChecks && prevCard && prevCard.checks) {
    mergedChecks = Object.assign({}, prevCard.checks);
    if (mergedChecks.conclusion == null) mergedChecks.carried = true;
}
```

- A **terminal** carried record (`conclusion != null`) carries as-is, unmarked — it is a resolved verdict (asserted in the existing fallback test).
- An **active** carried record rides marked — a merged card can no longer read "validation in flight" for the whole 24h window (new test: carried `in_progress` record with `conclusion: null` → `checks.carried === true`, runId preserved).
- A fresh cite from the runs list still wins over any carried record (unchanged, already tested).
- The audit fields stay uniform across cite/auxiliary/carried records (all `runCite`-shaped — see thread 4), and the shape is now documented in the module-header schema note.

`run_factoryState` 100/0.

